       39  The '''Dubăsari District''' ({{IPAc-ro|lang|pron|D|u|b|ă|'|s|a|ri}}) is a [[Administrative divisions of Moldova|district]] in the east of [[Moldova]], with the administrative center at [[Cocieri]]. As of the [[2024 Moldovan census]], its population was 21,781. This does not include the 715 people th
       40  ==History==
       41  The territory which today is part of [[Dubăsari]] district has been inhabited since the [[Stone Age]] (50–30000 years BC). Location of the earliest documentary attestation of the district is [[Corjova, Dubăsari|Corjova]], first attested in 1362. Other town with old certificate is [[Holercani]] villa
       42  ==Geography==
       43  Dubăsari district is located in the central part of Moldova. It has proximity to: [[Orhei District]] in north west, south-west [[Criuleni District]], [[Dubăsari sub-district|Dubăsari District (separatist territory)]] in the east. The landscape is predominantly plain (Dniester Middle Plain), but is i
       44  ===Climate===
       45  The climate is of a transition from [[maritime climate]] of [[Western Europe]], to temperate-[[Continental climate|continental]] [[Eastern Europe]]. Summer is warm and long, with average temperature of {{convert|22|°C|°F|abbr=on}} in July and the winter is mild with average January temperature {{con
       46  ===Fauna===
       47  The fauna is typical of Central Europe and includes [[fox]], [[hedgehog]], [[wild boar]], [[deer]], [[Lynx|wild cat]], [[otter]], [[mink]], [[raccoon dog]] and others. Of birds there are [[duck|wild duck]], [[egret]], [[crow]], [[quail]], [[starling]], [[swallow]] and more.
       48  ===Flora===
       49  Forests occupy 7.5% of the district and include [[oak]], [[hornbeam]], [[Silver linden|linden]], [[Ash (Fraxinus)|ash]], [[maple]] and others. [[Plant]]s include [[fescue]], [[mugwort]], [[Campanula|bell]], [[lentils]] and more.
       50  ===Rivers===
       51  Dubăsari district is located in the [[Dniester]] river basin. Nistru crosses district from north to south. In 1954 following the construction of [[Dubăsari hydroelectric power plant]], was formed [[Dubăsari Reservoir]], with an area of {{cvt|68|km2}} and a length of {{cvt|128|km}}.
       52  ==Administrative subdivisions==
       53  [[File:Rejon Dubosary.png|thumb|Dubăsari district administrative map (green: the territory controlled by the [[Republic of Moldova]], violet: territory controlled by [[Transnistria|separatists]])]]
       54  This is the only district in Moldova without cities. There are a total of 15 localities: 11 communes (containing further 4 villages within):
       70  [[Ustia, Dubăsari|Ustia]], [[Holercani]], [[Marcăuți, Dubăsari|Marcăuți]], [[Oxentea]], and [[Molovata]] are situated on the western (right) bank of the river [[Nistru]], while the other 10 villages on the eastern bank. Six of the latter ([[Cocieri]], {{ill|Vasilievca, Dubăsari|lt=Vasilievca|ro}}, [
       71  The village of Vasilievca, as well as considerable parts of the farmland of the villages of [[Cocieri]], Roghi, and Doroțcaia are situated east of the [[Tiraspol]]–[[Dubăsari]]–[[Rîbnița]] road.
